1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,333
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:02,333 --> 00:00:03,666
[screeching with effort]

3
00:00:11,166 --> 00:00:13,000
[yelping]

4
00:00:16,750 --> 00:00:19,500
Do not be afraid to fail, Riyu,

5
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:21,500
for every time we fail,

6
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:22,750
we learn.

7
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:24,166
[grumbling]

8
00:00:24,166 --> 00:00:27,625
Has anyone seen Cole,
Kai, or Frak?

9
00:00:27,625 --> 00:00:29,958
When I sent them elsewhere
to train,

10
00:00:29,958 --> 00:00:32,583
I didn't mean for forever.

11
00:00:34,166 --> 00:00:35,666
[Frak] How is it night already?

12
00:00:35,666 --> 00:00:37,916
It felt like we barely
had any sun today.

13
00:00:37,916 --> 00:00:39,333
Are we there yet?

14
00:00:39,333 --> 00:00:41,791
[Kai] Yeah, I thought
Master Wu's ghost or whatever

15
00:00:41,791 --> 00:00:43,041
showed you where this thing was.

16
00:00:43,041 --> 00:00:44,375
I was hearing his call.

17
00:00:44,375 --> 00:00:46,458
It's not like the ghost voice
drew me a map!

18
00:00:46,458 --> 00:00:48,291
The terrain out here
seems different.

19
00:00:48,291 --> 00:00:49,708
Could the Realms
still be shifting

20
00:00:49,708 --> 00:00:50,666
after the Merge?

21
00:00:50,666 --> 00:00:51,750
[Kai] Who knows?

22
00:00:51,750 --> 00:00:53,791
Maybe that explains
why it's dark out already.

23
00:00:55,416 --> 00:00:57,666
There! That's it!

24
00:00:58,708 --> 00:01:01,416
[♪♪♪]

25
00:01:07,333 --> 00:01:09,291
Looks like
there was an epic party here

26
00:01:09,291 --> 00:01:10,791
a long time ago,

27
00:01:10,791 --> 00:01:12,791
or maybe a battle.

28
00:01:12,791 --> 00:01:14,333
One of the two.

29
00:01:16,166 --> 00:01:17,625
Huh.

30
00:01:17,625 --> 00:01:18,791
[wincing] Ah!

31
00:01:19,791 --> 00:01:21,125
The feeling's so strong here.

32
00:01:21,125 --> 00:01:22,916
The Earth itself is crying out.

33
00:01:24,833 --> 00:01:26,500
This has to be
where it's coming from.

34
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:29,333
Maybe what I couldn't do
by myself,

35
00:01:29,333 --> 00:01:30,291
we can do together.

36
00:01:31,583 --> 00:01:33,083
Hope this works...

37
00:01:33,083 --> 00:01:35,041
unless whatever
you're pulling up is evil,

38
00:01:35,041 --> 00:01:36,625
in which case, I hope you fail.

39
00:01:36,625 --> 00:01:37,875
No way Master Wu's voice

40
00:01:37,875 --> 00:01:40,000
would try to get Cole
to dig up something evil.

41
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,166
I mean, right?

42
00:01:41,166 --> 00:01:42,958
Master Wu apparently
caused the Merge

43
00:01:42,958 --> 00:01:45,291
for some reason, so who knows?

44
00:01:45,291 --> 00:01:46,625
[munching and gagging]

45
00:01:46,625 --> 00:01:48,083
If you hate Geo's wafers
so much,

46
00:01:48,083 --> 00:01:49,541
why are you still eating them?

47
00:01:49,541 --> 00:01:52,041
[sighing] I keep hoping
they'll eventually taste good.

48
00:01:52,041 --> 00:01:54,041
[munching and coughing]

49
00:01:59,083 --> 00:02:00,916
There, Frak, can you feel it?

50
00:02:00,916 --> 00:02:02,208
There's something huge
down there.

51
00:02:02,208 --> 00:02:03,416
[gasping]

52
00:02:03,416 --> 00:02:06,083
It's hard to sense anything
over all the screaming--

53
00:02:06,083 --> 00:02:07,625
Wait, is this...?

54
00:02:07,625 --> 00:02:08,625
You got it.

55
00:02:08,625 --> 00:02:10,000
I feel your quake.

56
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,583
What could it be?

57
00:02:11,583 --> 00:02:13,750
Oh, it's massive.

58
00:02:13,750 --> 00:02:15,333
Only one way to find out.

59
00:02:15,333 --> 00:02:16,416
Pull!

60
00:02:16,416 --> 00:02:17,916
[ground crumbling]

61
00:02:20,708 --> 00:02:22,458
I think it's working.

62
00:02:22,458 --> 00:02:23,750
[straining]

63
00:02:24,708 --> 00:02:25,708
Is it a jet?

64
00:02:25,708 --> 00:02:27,625
A-a-a building?

65
00:02:30,125 --> 00:02:32,583
Whoa...

66
00:02:32,583 --> 00:02:33,916
[munching and gagging]

67
00:02:35,916 --> 00:02:39,000
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

68
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,125
♪ Together we will rise ♪

69
00:02:42,125 --> 00:02:45,041
♪ We fight ♪

70
00:02:45,041 --> 00:02:48,666
♪ Be a ninja for what's right ♪

71
00:02:52,333 --> 00:02:53,833
[slurping]

72
00:02:53,833 --> 00:02:55,125
Ah...

73
00:02:55,125 --> 00:02:58,125
Moss milk ice cream
never tasted so good.

74
00:02:58,125 --> 00:03:00,041
A frozen delight.

75
00:03:00,041 --> 00:03:03,500
Sora, this stuff's
only okay at best.

76
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:05,875
Ah, I guess
barely escaping with your life

77
00:03:05,875 --> 00:03:07,083
from a crazed tiger dude

78
00:03:07,083 --> 00:03:09,541
who wants to shut you
into a Casket of Bones

79
00:03:09,541 --> 00:03:11,958
makes everything taste better.

80
00:03:11,958 --> 00:03:13,916
[slurping]

81
00:03:15,041 --> 00:03:17,083
Okay, I'm getting another one,

82
00:03:17,083 --> 00:03:18,916
but then we gotta find a way

83
00:03:18,916 --> 00:03:21,708
to help those poor hollow people
in Mysterium.

84
00:03:21,708 --> 00:03:22,916
Should we head back
to the Monastery

85
00:03:22,916 --> 00:03:24,291
and tell the others?

86
00:03:24,291 --> 00:03:25,625
Yeah...

87
00:03:25,625 --> 00:03:28,208
Not sure they're gonna
be happy to see me, though.

88
00:03:28,208 --> 00:03:29,416
Trust me,

89
00:03:29,416 --> 00:03:30,958
everyone misses you.

90
00:03:30,958 --> 00:03:34,083
Listen, there's somewhere
I need to go first.

91
00:03:34,083 --> 00:03:35,833
Only problem is,

92
00:03:35,833 --> 00:03:38,208
we can't get there on bikes.

93
00:03:38,208 --> 00:03:39,583
Let me see what I can do.

94
00:03:39,583 --> 00:03:42,125
[♪♪♪]

95
00:03:44,333 --> 00:03:46,666
[marching feet]

96
00:03:56,125 --> 00:03:58,708
I didn't even know
this place had weapons.

97
00:03:58,708 --> 00:04:00,125
I'm impressed.

98
00:04:00,125 --> 00:04:01,916
Thanks for giving us
a place to hide.

99
00:04:01,916 --> 00:04:02,958
Of course.

100
00:04:02,958 --> 00:04:04,250
It's an honor.

101
00:04:04,250 --> 00:04:06,541
We're from the suburbs
of Ninjago City.

102
00:04:06,541 --> 00:04:07,750
You've probably saved our lives

103
00:04:07,750 --> 00:04:09,625
more times than we can count.

104
00:04:09,625 --> 00:04:10,875
Our son,

105
00:04:10,875 --> 00:04:13,083
he loved you all so much.

106
00:04:13,083 --> 00:04:15,833
How did your Ninja survive
the obliteration of the Merge?

107
00:04:15,833 --> 00:04:17,791
There was no obliteration.

108
00:04:17,791 --> 00:04:20,708
Lee's been lying to you.

109
00:04:20,708 --> 00:04:21,750
Hmm.

110
00:04:21,750 --> 00:04:24,125
We'd started to suspect that,
to be honest.

111
00:04:24,125 --> 00:04:27,583
So the Merge didn't really
destroy the outside world?

112
00:04:27,583 --> 00:04:31,416
No. In fact, it brought
all the realms together.

113
00:04:31,416 --> 00:04:33,458
Ninjago survived,

114
00:04:33,458 --> 00:04:37,166
and so did someone else...

115
00:04:37,166 --> 00:04:38,583
your son.

116
00:04:38,583 --> 00:04:42,333
[gasping]
Arin's... alive?

117
00:04:43,708 --> 00:04:45,833
Oh! [crying and laughing]

118
00:04:50,041 --> 00:04:51,375
[ground rumbling]

119
00:04:51,375 --> 00:04:53,875
[grunting with effort]

120
00:04:56,125 --> 00:04:58,375
There must be a whole skeleton
down there!

121
00:04:58,375 --> 00:05:00,333
You've got to be kidding me.

122
00:05:00,333 --> 00:05:01,208
There's more?

123
00:05:01,208 --> 00:05:02,166
Take a break, you two.

124
00:05:02,166 --> 00:05:03,125
You're gonna burn out.

125
00:05:03,125 --> 00:05:04,750
[gasping]

126
00:05:04,750 --> 00:05:06,708
[groaning]

127
00:05:06,708 --> 00:05:07,666
[ground rumbling and cracking]

128
00:05:07,666 --> 00:05:09,666
No, no! We're losing ground!

129
00:05:13,083 --> 00:05:16,750
[straining]
I can't keep this up!

130
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:18,458
[grunting and gasping]

131
00:05:18,458 --> 00:05:19,541
You've hit hard pack...

132
00:05:20,708 --> 00:05:22,958
but don't worry, I'm here.

133
00:05:28,041 --> 00:05:31,166
H'yah! Ha! Ha! Ha!

134
00:05:33,708 --> 00:05:35,541
Maybe we can do this after all.

135
00:05:37,416 --> 00:05:38,791
In my vision,

136
00:05:38,791 --> 00:05:40,166
the Source Dragons were talking

137
00:05:40,166 --> 00:05:42,333
like ThunderFang
was still alive,

138
00:05:42,333 --> 00:05:45,125
but Arin released the souls
that empowered him.

139
00:05:45,125 --> 00:05:47,791
We saw ThunderFang turn to dust.

140
00:05:47,791 --> 00:05:50,208
Yeah, yeah,
sounds like a big problem.

141
00:05:50,208 --> 00:05:52,666
I'm thinking about
our small problem.

142
00:05:52,666 --> 00:05:54,541
Mr. Ball-of-Handsome there

143
00:05:54,541 --> 00:05:56,458
is looking more rested
by the second,

144
00:05:56,458 --> 00:05:58,750
and then he's gonna start
tentacling our brains.

145
00:05:58,750 --> 00:06:01,458
How do we get out?

146
00:06:01,458 --> 00:06:03,416
Oh, wait, I got it!

147
00:06:03,416 --> 00:06:06,166
Ah, should've
thought of this before!

148
00:06:06,166 --> 00:06:07,291
What is that?

149
00:06:07,291 --> 00:06:09,333
Our escape!

150
00:06:09,333 --> 00:06:11,291
Wait for it...
[chuckling awkwardly]

151
00:06:12,250 --> 00:06:13,291
[snoring]

152
00:06:13,291 --> 00:06:14,333
[WyldFyre grunting]

153
00:06:14,333 --> 00:06:15,625
What's taking so long?

154
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:16,875
Just work!

155
00:06:16,875 --> 00:06:18,291
[groaning in frustration]
You stupid thing!

156
00:06:18,291 --> 00:06:19,291
H'yah!

157
00:06:21,208 --> 00:06:22,625
[gate clanking open]

158
00:06:22,625 --> 00:06:24,583
Yes! Plan B worked!

159
00:06:24,583 --> 00:06:25,583
"Plan B"?

160
00:06:25,583 --> 00:06:27,375
You just hurled that thing
in anger.

161
00:06:27,375 --> 00:06:30,291
Hurling stuff in anger
is always my Plan B,

162
00:06:30,291 --> 00:06:32,250
even when it's also my Plan A.

163
00:06:32,250 --> 00:06:33,291
Come on!

164
00:06:33,291 --> 00:06:35,708
[♪♪♪]

165
00:06:35,708 --> 00:06:37,375
Arin's been searching for you

166
00:06:37,375 --> 00:06:38,916
ever since the Merge happened.

167
00:06:38,916 --> 00:06:41,000
We came here to find you.

168
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,625
So Arin's here too?

169
00:06:42,625 --> 00:06:44,333
He, uh...

170
00:06:44,333 --> 00:06:47,458
His investigation took him
in another direction.

171
00:06:47,458 --> 00:06:49,083
[Jay scoffs]

172
00:06:51,708 --> 00:06:53,541
Well, we've actually
been doing

173
00:06:53,541 --> 00:06:55,583
a little investigation
of our own.

174
00:06:55,583 --> 00:06:59,916
We call it the "Mystery
of the Mood-Changing Neighbors."

175
00:06:59,916 --> 00:07:02,791
Barry and I have been
suspicious of Lee's story

176
00:07:02,791 --> 00:07:03,958
for a while,

177
00:07:03,958 --> 00:07:06,458
but anyone
who openly questions Lee

178
00:07:06,458 --> 00:07:07,625
disappears,

179
00:07:07,625 --> 00:07:09,166
and comes back days later

180
00:07:09,166 --> 00:07:11,458
with all their doubts... gone.

181
00:07:11,458 --> 00:07:12,500
Mm-hmm.

182
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:14,833
You think Lee
is doing something to them?

183
00:07:14,833 --> 00:07:16,291
Altering their minds?

184
00:07:16,291 --> 00:07:18,750
Jay, you said
the Administration checked

185
00:07:18,750 --> 00:07:20,291
for all kinds of mind control.

186
00:07:20,291 --> 00:07:21,166
They did.

187
00:07:21,166 --> 00:07:22,458
On a wide scale,

188
00:07:22,458 --> 00:07:24,375
but if Lee's
only using it selectively

189
00:07:24,375 --> 00:07:25,583
on one or two people,

190
00:07:25,583 --> 00:07:28,041
the Administration
wouldn't have detected it.

191
00:07:28,041 --> 00:07:29,833
What's the Administration?

192
00:07:29,833 --> 00:07:32,041
Let's worry about
one thing at a time.

193
00:07:32,041 --> 00:07:34,375
There's an off-limits
backstage area

194
00:07:34,375 --> 00:07:35,416
in this cavern.

195
00:07:35,416 --> 00:07:37,833
We think Lee's
bringing the neighbors there.

196
00:07:37,833 --> 00:07:39,125
[Jay] We've been back there.

197
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:40,416
It was definitely weird,

198
00:07:40,416 --> 00:07:42,625
but we didn't see
any kidnappees.

199
00:07:42,625 --> 00:07:45,125
Might be worth looking
with Barry and Jenny's help.

200
00:07:45,125 --> 00:07:47,916
Maybe that's where Lloyd
and Wyldfyre are.

201
00:07:47,916 --> 00:07:50,208
Okay,
so this backstage entrance

202
00:07:50,208 --> 00:07:51,875
sees the most activity,

203
00:07:51,875 --> 00:07:54,000
but we haven't been able
to break in.

204
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,416
Leave that to me.

205
00:07:59,708 --> 00:08:01,916
This won't take long.

206
00:08:01,916 --> 00:08:04,416
I just... want to say goodbye.

207
00:08:04,416 --> 00:08:06,500
Take all the time
you need, Arin.

208
00:08:16,583 --> 00:08:17,708
[gasping]

209
00:08:19,375 --> 00:08:20,333
What?

210
00:08:20,333 --> 00:08:22,916
Are their graves empty?

211
00:08:22,916 --> 00:08:25,291
If my parents aren't here,

212
00:08:25,291 --> 00:08:27,708
where are they?

213
00:08:29,666 --> 00:08:31,541
[Barry] Bad neighbors
are brought here.

214
00:08:31,541 --> 00:08:34,250
Sometimes it's days
before they come out again.

215
00:08:36,291 --> 00:08:38,333
I can easily take out
two guards,

216
00:08:38,333 --> 00:08:41,666
but alerting one Lee
alerts all Lees.

217
00:08:41,666 --> 00:08:44,125
Yup, many bodies, one mind.

218
00:08:44,125 --> 00:08:45,791
Jenny and I will lure him away

219
00:08:45,791 --> 00:08:47,791
while you and Barry sneak in.

220
00:08:49,125 --> 00:08:50,041
Be careful.

221
00:08:50,041 --> 00:08:51,958
You too.

222
00:08:54,916 --> 00:08:56,458
Excuse me,

223
00:08:56,458 --> 00:08:59,750
aren't those the Bad Neighbors
you're looking for?

224
00:08:59,750 --> 00:09:01,333
[wailing dramatically] Whoa!

225
00:09:01,333 --> 00:09:02,916
Thanks!

226
00:09:02,916 --> 00:09:06,708
It's neighbors like you
that give neighbors a good name.

227
00:09:07,791 --> 00:09:09,083
I gotta admit,

228
00:09:09,083 --> 00:09:10,875
you're different
than I thought you'd be.

229
00:09:10,875 --> 00:09:11,958
[Jay] We knew each other?

230
00:09:11,958 --> 00:09:13,458
Well, not personally,

231
00:09:13,458 --> 00:09:15,291
but the Ninja are famous.

232
00:09:15,291 --> 00:09:17,291
My son had a poster of you
up on his wall,

233
00:09:17,291 --> 00:09:20,083
and my wife was a big fan
of your old game show.

234
00:09:20,083 --> 00:09:22,583
Why would a Ninja
host a game show?

235
00:09:22,583 --> 00:09:23,958
That sounds fake.

236
00:09:23,958 --> 00:09:24,875
[crackling]

237
00:09:24,875 --> 00:09:25,708
[beeping]

238
00:09:30,416 --> 00:09:31,541
And Arin said

239
00:09:31,541 --> 00:09:34,083
one time you got trapped
in a videogame...

240
00:09:34,083 --> 00:09:35,500
[laughing] and became
a rocking superstar!

241
00:09:35,500 --> 00:09:36,458
Oh, and when--

242
00:09:36,458 --> 00:09:38,791
[Jay] Now you're just
making things up.

243
00:09:40,291 --> 00:09:43,166
Sorry, but this area
is for cast members only.

244
00:09:43,166 --> 00:09:45,125
It's off-limits to Neighbors.

245
00:09:45,125 --> 00:09:47,458
Not for any secret,
nefarious reason--

246
00:09:47,458 --> 00:09:48,833
[crashing]

247
00:09:48,833 --> 00:09:50,791
[roaring]

248
00:09:51,875 --> 00:09:53,541
What are you doing here?

249
00:09:53,541 --> 00:09:55,583
Uh, rescuing you.

250
00:09:55,583 --> 00:09:57,750
[snorting] I rescued me.

251
00:09:57,750 --> 00:09:58,750
And him.

252
00:09:58,750 --> 00:10:01,250
[gasping]
You knocked out a Lee.

253
00:10:01,250 --> 00:10:02,958
Lee will not like that.

254
00:10:02,958 --> 00:10:04,750
More of him
will already be on the way.

255
00:10:04,750 --> 00:10:07,416
[gasping] You're Arin's dad!

256
00:10:07,416 --> 00:10:10,500
You have no idea
how good it is to meet you.

257
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:13,666
Hey, the Legendary Green Ninja!

258
00:10:13,666 --> 00:10:14,666
Intros later!

259
00:10:14,666 --> 00:10:17,083
Things are about to get
way Lee up in here!

260
00:10:21,750 --> 00:10:23,916
So glad you and Jay
had each other

261
00:10:23,916 --> 00:10:25,125
through the Merge.

262
00:10:25,125 --> 00:10:26,875
Don't know what Barry and I
would have done

263
00:10:26,875 --> 00:10:27,958
without each other.

264
00:10:27,958 --> 00:10:29,208
Funny you say that.

265
00:10:29,208 --> 00:10:31,333
I only just found Jay.

266
00:10:31,333 --> 00:10:32,708
He lost his memories,

267
00:10:32,708 --> 00:10:34,750
and doesn't even remember
who I am.

268
00:10:34,750 --> 00:10:35,791
Really?

269
00:10:35,791 --> 00:10:38,000
That's not
what his body language says,

270
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,708
and as an amateur detective,

271
00:10:39,708 --> 00:10:41,333
I study body language.

272
00:10:41,333 --> 00:10:43,708
What does his body language
tell you?

273
00:10:43,708 --> 00:10:46,208
That maybe his mind
doesn't remember you,

274
00:10:46,208 --> 00:10:47,583
but his heart sure does.

275
00:10:48,583 --> 00:10:49,458
[alerts beeping]

276
00:10:49,458 --> 00:10:50,333
[gasping]

277
00:10:58,458 --> 00:10:59,500
[Lees] Neighbors!

278
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:02,375
Please return to your homes
for an emergency,

279
00:11:02,375 --> 00:11:04,125
um, street cleaning.

280
00:11:04,125 --> 00:11:07,791
[Neighbors murmuring]

281
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,541
We need to meet up with Nya
and get to the elevator.

282
00:11:14,541 --> 00:11:16,125
What about
the other residents?

283
00:11:16,125 --> 00:11:18,625
Not paying me
to rescue everyone.

284
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:25,375
Imposters!

285
00:11:25,375 --> 00:11:27,416
Here to ruin everything!

286
00:11:27,416 --> 00:11:30,250
This is all
just so unneighborly!

287
00:11:30,250 --> 00:11:32,125
[clamoring angrily]

288
00:11:35,083 --> 00:11:37,750
Guess the only way out
is through.

289
00:11:37,750 --> 00:11:38,583
Love that!

290
00:11:38,583 --> 00:11:41,291
Eat fireball, Lee! H'yah!

291
00:11:41,291 --> 00:11:44,083
[yelping]

292
00:11:44,083 --> 00:11:46,208
I'm starting to like you.

293
00:11:47,291 --> 00:11:49,000
Ah!

294
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,916
H'yah! [grunting]

295
00:11:52,041 --> 00:11:53,833
Ah! Oof!

296
00:11:55,583 --> 00:11:56,666
Guess I'll never get to finish

297
00:11:56,666 --> 00:11:59,000
that needlepoint class
I started.

298
00:12:03,125 --> 00:12:06,041
I... I don't understand.

299
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:09,166
Where'd those guys come from?

300
00:12:09,166 --> 00:12:10,166
Beats me!

301
00:12:10,166 --> 00:12:11,875
Maybe they have some answers!

302
00:12:11,875 --> 00:12:13,250
Hey, you guys!

303
00:12:13,250 --> 00:12:14,916
What's going on?

304
00:12:14,916 --> 00:12:16,500
Oh, no, you don't!

305
00:12:20,666 --> 00:12:22,000
An elevator shaft?

306
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:23,458
[clanking]

307
00:12:23,458 --> 00:12:25,125
[♪♪♪]

308
00:12:28,125 --> 00:12:29,083
What?

309
00:12:29,083 --> 00:12:31,000
This place is amazing,

310
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,208
but probably evil,
given our luck.

311
00:12:33,208 --> 00:12:34,875
[crowd clamoring below]

312
00:12:34,875 --> 00:12:36,916
Look, some kind of street fight.

313
00:12:40,750 --> 00:12:43,250
Are those... the Ninja?

314
00:12:43,250 --> 00:12:44,583
-H'yah!
-Ah!

315
00:12:44,583 --> 00:12:45,791
Ow!

316
00:12:47,583 --> 00:12:49,750
[grunts of pain and impact]

317
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:55,583
[grunting]

318
00:12:55,583 --> 00:12:57,500
The Lees can out-teamwork us.

319
00:12:57,500 --> 00:12:59,250
We have to divide
their attention!

320
00:12:59,250 --> 00:13:01,791
For once, don't work together!

321
00:13:01,791 --> 00:13:04,041
I do my best work solo.

322
00:13:04,041 --> 00:13:05,333
H'yah!

323
00:13:07,791 --> 00:13:09,666
[dragon snarling]

324
00:13:12,250 --> 00:13:14,166
[beeping]

325
00:13:15,041 --> 00:13:15,875
[Lee groaning]

326
00:13:17,208 --> 00:13:19,041
I'll be taking this, thank you.

327
00:13:19,041 --> 00:13:19,875
[Lee yelping] Whoa!

328
00:13:26,166 --> 00:13:27,541
[Lees yelping] Whoa-oh!

329
00:13:29,833 --> 00:13:30,875
[Lees yelping]

330
00:13:32,250 --> 00:13:35,916
[♪♪♪]

331
00:13:35,916 --> 00:13:39,250
If the Ninja are here,
they're helping people...

332
00:13:39,250 --> 00:13:41,583
what I should have been doing
instead of following Ras.

333
00:13:41,583 --> 00:13:43,166
Don't be so hard on yourself.

334
00:13:43,166 --> 00:13:45,041
You only did that
for your parents.

335
00:13:46,166 --> 00:13:47,416
My parents!

336
00:13:47,416 --> 00:13:49,250
Yeah, that's what I said.

337
00:13:49,250 --> 00:13:50,583
No, look!

338
00:13:50,583 --> 00:13:52,250
My parents!

339
00:13:54,166 --> 00:13:56,250
Lloyd found them.

340
00:13:58,958 --> 00:14:00,416
[smashing]

341
00:14:01,208 --> 00:14:03,583
Whoa! You okay, Mister?

342
00:14:06,375 --> 00:14:08,125
How'd you get here?

343
00:14:08,125 --> 00:14:09,375
Not really the best time

344
00:14:09,375 --> 00:14:11,916
to start
a New Neighbor Orientation,

345
00:14:11,916 --> 00:14:12,958
but okay.

346
00:14:12,958 --> 00:14:16,250
♪ Perhaps you're
feeling in the dumps... ♪

347
00:14:17,083 --> 00:14:18,375
Yeah, let's wait

348
00:14:18,375 --> 00:14:20,125
until I can get my other bodies
to harmonize.

349
00:14:20,125 --> 00:14:21,583
It'll sound much better.

350
00:14:21,583 --> 00:14:23,125
"Other bodies"?

351
00:14:23,125 --> 00:14:24,500
[ground rumbling,
straining with effort]

352
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:26,833
I think... this is... it!

353
00:14:26,833 --> 00:14:29,333
[all roaring and straining]

354
00:14:29,333 --> 00:14:31,791
[gasping]

355
00:14:31,791 --> 00:14:33,041
You did it!

356
00:14:33,041 --> 00:14:35,458
[panting] We... did it.

357
00:14:35,458 --> 00:14:37,208
This dragon
makes the Firstbourne

358
00:14:37,208 --> 00:14:38,375
look like a pup.

359
00:14:38,375 --> 00:14:40,125
It can only be
one thing, right?

360
00:14:46,333 --> 00:14:48,666
The remains
of a dead Source Dragon.

361
00:14:48,666 --> 00:14:49,958
Whoa!

362
00:14:49,958 --> 00:14:50,958
[gasping]

363
00:14:50,958 --> 00:14:51,833
Huh?

364
00:14:56,208 --> 00:14:58,250
<i>What was once lost...</i>

365
00:14:58,250 --> 00:15:00,458
<i>can now be found...</i>

366
00:15:00,458 --> 00:15:02,291
Master Wu?

367
00:15:04,666 --> 00:15:05,666
[shouting]

368
00:15:05,666 --> 00:15:07,750
[slamming and grunting]

369
00:15:08,916 --> 00:15:09,791
Greetings, Neighbor!

370
00:15:09,791 --> 00:15:11,000
Just going door to door

371
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,583
assuring Neighbors
that everything is fine.

372
00:15:13,583 --> 00:15:14,583
Oh, uh, one moment.

373
00:15:14,583 --> 00:15:15,583
[grunting]

374
00:15:18,083 --> 00:15:19,541
Nothing to worry about.

375
00:15:21,375 --> 00:15:23,125
[grunting]

376
00:15:24,875 --> 00:15:26,000
[yelping]

377
00:15:28,708 --> 00:15:30,375
[Lloyd] This isn't
getting us anywhere.

378
00:15:31,666 --> 00:15:33,416
[Jay] Speak for yourself!

379
00:15:34,375 --> 00:15:35,208
Whoa!

380
00:15:40,458 --> 00:15:41,291
[gasping]

381
00:15:42,166 --> 00:15:44,041
Aah!

382
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:46,916
[groaning] I should have
seen that coming.

383
00:15:46,916 --> 00:15:49,291
I'm gonna punch you so hard!

384
00:15:49,291 --> 00:15:50,583
Like a single punch

385
00:15:50,583 --> 00:15:53,500
could take down
a stone-cold warrior like me!

386
00:15:56,583 --> 00:15:57,708
That's cheating.

387
00:15:59,166 --> 00:16:00,791
[screaming]

388
00:16:01,625 --> 00:16:05,333
Why... isn't...
this... thing... working?

389
00:16:08,458 --> 00:16:09,375
[smashing]

390
00:16:11,291 --> 00:16:12,291
Aah!

391
00:16:12,291 --> 00:16:13,875
[thudding heavily]

392
00:16:16,375 --> 00:16:18,125
Why'd you save me?

393
00:16:18,125 --> 00:16:20,416
You're from the outside world.

394
00:16:20,416 --> 00:16:21,625
You don't need me.

395
00:16:21,625 --> 00:16:23,708
I need you not to be crushed.

396
00:16:23,708 --> 00:16:24,583
Why?

397
00:16:24,583 --> 00:16:26,625
'Cause a nice, normal person

398
00:16:26,625 --> 00:16:28,000
wants people to be okay,

399
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,583
and not be crushed
by falling debris.

400
00:16:30,583 --> 00:16:33,041
You don't spend a lot of time
with other people or something?

401
00:16:33,041 --> 00:16:35,500
[Lee] I never met another person
until the Merge.

402
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:37,625
Did you build this place?

403
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:40,666
Why?

404
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,916
Because I need people.

405
00:16:43,916 --> 00:16:46,041
<i>For so, so long,</i>

406
00:16:46,041 --> 00:16:47,250
<i>in the Realm of Lee,</i>

407
00:16:47,250 --> 00:16:49,291
<i>there was only Lee.</i>

408
00:16:49,291 --> 00:16:51,250
<i>And Lee, and Lee,</i>

409
00:16:51,250 --> 00:16:52,958
<i>and Lee...</i>

410
00:17:05,708 --> 00:17:07,375
<i>I tried to keep myself busy,</i>

411
00:17:07,375 --> 00:17:09,375
<i>but no matter how many bodies</i>
<i>I created,</i>

412
00:17:09,375 --> 00:17:11,666
<i>there was only just me.</i>

413
00:17:14,083 --> 00:17:16,041
<i>Just Lee.</i>

414
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:22,500
<i>Then one day,</i>
<i>something remarkable happened.</i>

415
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:23,833
<i>I didn't know it at first,</i>

416
00:17:23,833 --> 00:17:27,250
<i>but the Realm of Lee</i>
<i>merged with other realms.</i>

417
00:17:27,250 --> 00:17:30,583
<i>Lee was no longer alone.</i>

418
00:17:37,166 --> 00:17:38,583
[grunting with effort]

419
00:17:38,583 --> 00:17:39,916
[gasping]

420
00:17:39,916 --> 00:17:42,458
Where... where am I?

421
00:17:42,458 --> 00:17:44,291
You're in Lee, of course!

422
00:17:44,291 --> 00:17:47,166
Wait, are there
other places to be?

423
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:51,791
<i>He was the first Non-Lee</i>
<i>I had ever met,</i>

424
00:17:51,791 --> 00:17:54,041
<i>a whole other person</i>

425
00:17:54,041 --> 00:17:56,416
<i>who had thoughts</i>
<i>that weren't my thoughts.</i>

426
00:17:57,375 --> 00:17:59,750
<i>Games are so much more fun</i>
<i>when you don't know</i>

427
00:17:59,750 --> 00:18:02,125
<i>what the other player</i>
<i>is going to do!</i>

428
00:18:03,416 --> 00:18:04,458
[laughing]

429
00:18:10,125 --> 00:18:12,166
<i>Life was all new.</i>

430
00:18:14,375 --> 00:18:16,583
[laughing] Wha! Whoa!

431
00:18:16,583 --> 00:18:17,583
Whuh-oh!

432
00:18:18,833 --> 00:18:19,791
[laughing] Oh!

433
00:18:19,791 --> 00:18:21,208
<i>I realized</i>

434
00:18:21,208 --> 00:18:24,333
<i>other people must be the key</i>
<i>to being happy.</i>

435
00:18:26,041 --> 00:18:28,041
<i>He told me</i>
<i>of the outside world,</i>

436
00:18:28,041 --> 00:18:29,208
<i>its wonders,</i>

437
00:18:29,208 --> 00:18:31,458
<i>and what he missed...</i>

438
00:18:31,458 --> 00:18:34,291
<i>until one day,</i>
<i>he missed them so much,</i>

439
00:18:34,291 --> 00:18:36,166
<i>he left Lee.</i>

440
00:18:38,291 --> 00:18:39,708
<i>I stayed,</i>

441
00:18:39,708 --> 00:18:43,458
<i>because there is no Lee</i>
<i>without... Lee.</i>

442
00:18:43,458 --> 00:18:45,375
[rain pouring]

443
00:18:46,625 --> 00:18:47,916
<i>Right then,</i>

444
00:18:47,916 --> 00:18:51,041
<i>I vowed to make</i>
<i>the Land of Lee so perfect,</i>

445
00:18:51,041 --> 00:18:53,666
<i>no one would ever</i>
<i>want to leave again.</i>

446
00:18:53,666 --> 00:18:56,875
[battle continuing]

447
00:18:56,875 --> 00:18:58,791
And I succeeded!

448
00:18:58,791 --> 00:19:00,250
Why else
would the Administration

449
00:19:00,250 --> 00:19:02,000
dump its unwanteds here?

450
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:06,208
I painted a wonderful
rainbow of lies

451
00:19:06,208 --> 00:19:08,666
so my new Neighbors
wouldn't ever be curious

452
00:19:08,666 --> 00:19:10,291
about what's outside,

453
00:19:10,291 --> 00:19:15,166
but these new outsiders
want to wash it all away!

454
00:19:15,166 --> 00:19:18,333
I won't let those Ninja
take my friends from me!

455
00:19:18,333 --> 00:19:20,583
I was alone once, too.

456
00:19:20,583 --> 00:19:21,708
A single lie

457
00:19:21,708 --> 00:19:23,375
pushed away
the first real friend

458
00:19:23,375 --> 00:19:25,000
I ever made.

459
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:27,083
Friends shouldn't
lie to friends,

460
00:19:27,083 --> 00:19:28,208
ever,

461
00:19:28,208 --> 00:19:31,250
but especially on, like,
a city-wide level.

462
00:19:31,250 --> 00:19:33,666
Well, if you have
a way of making friends

463
00:19:33,666 --> 00:19:36,458
that doesn't involve
mass deception and brainwashing,

464
00:19:36,458 --> 00:19:38,041
I'd like to hear it.

465
00:19:38,041 --> 00:19:40,083
[grunting with impact]

466
00:19:41,416 --> 00:19:44,250
Nya, one of us has to
grab Arin's parents and go--

467
00:19:44,250 --> 00:19:46,875
Oh, no, where are
Barry and Jenny?

468
00:19:50,458 --> 00:19:52,500
So you came here for those two?

469
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:55,458
Then I'll be sure
to keep them here forever!

470
00:19:56,458 --> 00:19:58,166
No!

471
00:20:00,208 --> 00:20:01,750
Another Ninja?

472
00:20:01,750 --> 00:20:02,875
I don't know this color.

473
00:20:02,875 --> 00:20:04,000
He must be new.

474
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,166
[grunting]

475
00:20:05,166 --> 00:20:08,208
I am a good friend.
I am a good friend!

476
00:20:11,625 --> 00:20:15,583
No, you're not being
a good friend right now,

477
00:20:15,583 --> 00:20:16,958
but you can be.

478
00:20:16,958 --> 00:20:19,000
Tell everyone the truth.

479
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,708
Let them go if they want,

480
00:20:20,708 --> 00:20:22,708
and maybe some will stay,

481
00:20:22,708 --> 00:20:25,291
and those will be real friends.

482
00:20:25,291 --> 00:20:27,041
I've only been here
a few minutes,

483
00:20:27,041 --> 00:20:29,833
and I think the Land of Lee
is pretty amazing.

484
00:20:29,833 --> 00:20:31,708
You-you do?

485
00:20:31,708 --> 00:20:32,791
For real?

486
00:20:35,250 --> 00:20:39,291
[♪♪♪]

487
00:20:47,041 --> 00:20:50,041
Mom? Dad?

488
00:20:53,458 --> 00:20:55,583
Arin!

489
00:20:55,583 --> 00:20:57,125
[sobbing joyfully]

490
00:21:03,166 --> 00:21:04,458
A new neighbor?

491
00:21:04,458 --> 00:21:06,458
The Administration
always drops them off

492
00:21:06,458 --> 00:21:07,458
above ground.

493
00:21:09,791 --> 00:21:12,791
Whatever you are,
get away from me!

494
00:21:14,041 --> 00:21:16,833
[spectral tone sounding]

495
00:21:18,583 --> 00:21:20,958
Is that... music?

496
00:21:20,958 --> 00:21:22,208
Oh, no.

497
00:21:22,208 --> 00:21:24,833
Not here. Not now.

498
00:21:26,916 --> 00:21:29,458
[wraiths shrieking]

499
00:21:31,833 --> 00:21:32,833
[spectral horn blowing]

500
00:21:37,208 --> 00:21:38,875
[Lees all moaning]

501
00:21:38,875 --> 00:21:42,583
<i>Look around and see...</i>

502
00:21:42,583 --> 00:21:46,833
<i>in the land of Lee...</i>

503
00:21:46,833 --> 00:21:48,625
<i>...look around...</i>

504
00:21:51,208 --> 00:21:52,833
[spectral horn blowing]

